The graph shows requests for four lunchtime activities.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=12mm,y=8mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[draw=black,->] (0,0)--(0,5.6);
\draw[draw=black,->] (0,0)--(5,0);
\foreach \y/\v in {0/0,1/5,2/10,3/15,4/20,5/25} {
\draw[draw=black] (-0.1,\y)--(0,\y);
\path (-0.15,\y) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};
}
\draw[draw=black] (0.5,0) rectangle (1.1,3);
\draw[draw=black] (1.6,0) rectangle (2.2,5);
\draw[draw=black] (2.7,0)--(3.3,0);
\draw[draw=black] (3.8,0) rectangle (4.4,2);
\foreach \x/\lab in {0.8/Art,1.9/Sport,3/Music,4.1/Chess} {
\path (\x,-0.15) node[below] {\lab};
}
\path (-0.9,2.7) node[rotate=90] {Requests};
\path (2.5,-0.9) node[below] {Activity};
\path (2.5,6.1) node {Lunchtime activity requests};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

(a) How many requests were there for Art?
(b) Which activity had the most requests? Which had the fewest?
(c) Which had more requests, Art or Chess?
(d) How many more requests were there for Sport than for Chess?

The graph shows the temperature in a classroom. What was the temperature at $11$ a.m.?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=13mm,y=8mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[draw=black!20,xstep=13mm,ystep=8mm] (0,0) grid (4,6);
\draw[draw=black,->] (0,0)--(0,6.5);
\draw[draw=black,->] (0,0)--(4.5,0);
\foreach \y/\v in {0/0,1/5,2/10,3/15,4/20,5/25,6/30} {
\draw[draw=black] (-0.1,\y)--(0,\y);
\path (-0.15,\y) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};
}
\foreach \x/\lab in {0/{9 a.m.},1/{10 a.m.},2/{11 a.m.},3/{12 noon},4/{1 p.m.}} {
\draw[draw=black] (\x,0)--(\x,-0.1);
\path (\x,-0.15) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {\lab};
}
\definecolor{seriesblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[draw=seriesblue,thick] (0,2)--(1,3)--(2,4)--(3,5)--(4,3);
\foreach \x/\y in {0/2,1/3,2/4,3/5,4/3} {
\fill[seriesblue] (\x,\y) circle (1.8pt);
}
\path (-0.9,3) node[rotate=90] {Temperature ($^\circ$C)};
\path (2,-0.85) node[below] {Time};
\path (2,6.9) node {Classroom temperature};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
